<title>GERMANY: Volkswagen /EC dispute nearing end - Bonn.</title>
<headline>Volkswagen /EC dispute nearing end - Bonn.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Negotiations to resolve a subsidy dispute between Volkswagen AG and the European Commission have entered the final phase, a German Economics Ministry spokeswoman said on Friday.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said the talks now centered on technical legal points and that the government is confident that remaining issues can be resolved by late summer.</p>
<p>At issue is 140 million marks ($75.1 million) of subsidies that VW has received from the German state of Saxony, a large portion of which had not been approved by European competition authorities.</p>
<p>Commission spokeswoman Sarah Lambert said on Thursday that various scenarios to resolve the dispute were being discussed and called a German newspaper report that a deal was close &quot;slightly premature&quot;.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom + 49 228 26097150 ($ = 1.865 German Marks)</p>
